# Private functions
  @fn periodTicks(period, resolution)  @ 26-29
  @fn retrig(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 33-52
      @contract  retrig tiles the host window with evenly-spaced same-pitch fxNotes; every hit is derived  @ 31
      @contract  velocity ramps params.ramp per tile from the host vel, clamped 1..127; detune inherited verbatim  @ 32
  @fn trill(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 55-76
      @contract  trill alternates host pitch with a note `step` scale-steps away (via ctx.step); every hit derived  @ 54
  @fn playingAt(events, t)  @ 79-88
      -- Notes sounding at logical tick `t`, ascending by realised pitch (semitone*100 + detune cents).
  @fn arpIndex(count, dir, i)  @ 92-100
      -- Which voice of the active set step `i` plays, by direction. updown bounces without
      -- repeating the extremes (span 2*(n-1)); up/down wrap.
  @fn arp(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 105-125
      @contract  arp samples the sounding notes at each step (period QN), playing one by `dir`  @ 102
      @contract  dir up|down|updown cycles the current active set; an empty active set -> a rest  @ 103
      @contract  hits abut (endppq = next step), clamped to the window; vel/detune from the voice  @ 104
  @fn ostinato(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 129-150
      @contract  ostinato gates the sounding region notes by a stored pattern -- pattern gives onset/dur/vel, each voice its pitch/detune  @ 127
      @contract  every voice sounding at a gate onset emits (none -> rest); the pattern loops from the window start; no lengthPpq -> inert  @ 128
  @fn chordStamp(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 157-175
      -- Voices carry true temper-step detune (intent); on one channel only lane 1's detune realises via pb, so a
      -- microtonal chord sounds faithfully only in 12-ET -- the hand-authored-chord limit. see docs/tuning.md
  @fn sine(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 180-200
      @contract  sine -> delta breakpoints in the dest's own units; depth at 1/period QN, unit-naive  @ 177
      @contract  breakpoints at sine extrema, 'slow'-shaped; linear ramp-in over onset QN  @ 178
      @contract  returns to 0 (the delta's rest) at window end -- no residual offset on the channel  @ 179
  @fn interval(a, b)  @ 204-206
      -- Cents between two notes' realised pitches. The microtonal offset already rides
      -- in detune, so this is pure note arithmetic -- no temper needed.
  @fn slide(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 211-241
      @contract  slide glide-in -> lane-1 pb-delta; slur to target over `over` QN; re-centres at end  @ 208
      @contract  target 'next' = interval to next same-lane note; 'fixed' = params.cents; pb-range clamps  @ 209
      @contract  no next note or unison target -> empty delta (channel untouched)  @ 210
  @fn curveAt(points, a)  @ 244-254
      -- Linear-interpolated normalized value at authored ppq `a`; points ascend in ppq, edges clamp flat.
  @fn lfo(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 259-287
      @contract  lfo tiles a normalized curve at 1/period QN, offset + scale map each val, unit-naive  @ 256
      @contract  breakpoints are a displacement from the dest's rest, which the augment fold lays them on  @ 257
      @contract  each cycle stretches the body lengthPpq -> period ticks; both window edges seeded  @ 258
  @fn velPattern(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 291-308
      @contract  velPattern rewrites stream-note velocities by a pattern; other fields carry verbatim  @ 289
      @contract  pattern steps per distinct onset (a chord shares one step) and cycles; vel clamps 1..127  @ 290
  -- Generator registry
  -- Dest: a per-entry target, and what each target's numbers mean
  -- Region park predicate + windows
  -- Curve thinning (freeze to group)
  @fn ridesLinear(p)  @ 567
      -- A shape governs the segment to its *right*, so a point is safe to lose only if it and its
      -- predecessor both ride linearly; a missing shape counts as non-linear. see design/fx-freeze.md § Freeze to group

# Public API (generators.*)
  @api generators.destOf(params)  @ 425-428
  @api generators.destProfile(dest)  @ 432-439
      -- Polarity is the controller's own, and its default rest says it: one resting mid-scale swings
      -- both ways, one at a rail only runs inward. An fx.rest override steers the fold seed, never this.
  @api generators.restFor(dest, override)  @ 442-444
      -- The resting base a continuous augment sums onto: an authored override wins, else the dest's rest.
  @api generators.destsFor(kind)  @ 447-454
      -- Every dest a kind can serve. Fewer than two is no choice at all, and earns no Dest row.
  @api generators.fieldRange(fd, dest)  @ 458-464
      -- A field's bounds in the target's own units: a magnitude spans rest outwards as far as the dest
      -- swings -- both ways if signed; anything else is fixed-unit and carries its bounds on the descriptor.
  @api generators.fieldsFor(entry)  @ 470-476
      -- The rows a stage shows: a synthesised Dest row where the kind can serve more than one target,
      -- then the kind's own fields. Synthesised once here rather than repeated per registry entry.
  @api generators.seed(kind)  @ 480-490
      -- A kind's default entry: the dest it seeds from, its fixed-unit defaults, and every quantity field
      -- resolved against that dest -- so one `frac` declaration reads correctly wherever it lands.
  @api generators.retarget(entry, dest)  @ 494-504
      -- Point an entry at another dest, carrying its magnitudes over as the same proportion of the new
      -- target's swing. Equal references (CC 10 -> CC 8, both resting at 64) leave every value untouched.
  @api generators.parksNotes(region)  @ 510-515
      -- A region parks its covered chord iff it carries a note-dest kind: the chain's final note stream
      -- stands in for the members (ownership by dest, not mode). A husk (no kinds) parks nothing.
  @api generators.continuousTargets(fx)  @ 519-526
      -- Continuous targets a chain touches: set keyed 'pb' | <cc number>, empty for a pure-note
      -- chain -- phase 5's per-target scopes key off it. see design/interval-dirt.md § phase 5
  @api generators.chainDestType(fx, target)  @ 530-536
      -- The fold mode a chain presents for one continuous target: replace if any stage targeting it
      -- replaces, else augment -- drives cross-chain layering (a later replace wins). see design/note-macros-v2.md § The fx chain
  @api generators.parkWindows(regions)  @ 541-561
      -- The single source for "what 4.5 parks over": a note window for a discrete-replace chord, a cc window
      -- per continuous cc target and a pb window per continuous pb target (both replace or augment).
  @api generators.thinCurve(points, tol)  @ 573-613
      -- Douglas-Peucker, measuring vertical deviation rather than perpendicular distance: perpendicular
      -- would need a ticks-per-cent aspect ratio, under which "tolerance in cents" means nothing.
      @contract  returns a new array of the input point tables themselves -- selects, never invents  @ 571
      @contract  tol bounds vertical error in the curve's own value unit; > tol keeps, == tol collapses  @ 572

